VALUES ('ARCH-001-australia', 'ARCH-001', 'Australia', 'High', 52000, 78000, 'AUD 80k-120k/year', 'Taxable', 'Skilled Independent visa (subclass 189), Skilled Nominated (190), Skilled Work Regional (491), Employer Nomination Scheme (186); AACA skills assessment required', NULL, 'AACA National Program of Assessment (NPA); then Architectural Practice Examination (APE) with state/territory Architects Registration Board (ARB)', 'APE (Architectural Practice Examination) — 2-part competency assessment', 'IELTS 6.0+ (Academic) or equivalent', 18, 'AACA National Program of Assessment; APE; state ARB registration', ARRAY['Residential design', 'sustainable/green architecture', 'urban infill', 'aged care facilities', 'educational buildings'], 'Architects on Australia''s skilled occupation shortage list — eligible for multiple visa subclasses. NPA applications open Feb and Aug annually. AACA assesses overseas qualifications against 2021 National Standard of Competency for Architects. After NPA pass, must apply to state ARB for APE. 3 months minimum employment for Tasmania nomination (fast-track option). PR pathway makes Australia very attractive long-term.', 'APE pass rates not 100%; allow 18-24 months from arrival to full registration', 'AACA 2025; deltaimmigration.com.au; Jobs and Skills Australia')
