VALUES ('ARCH-001-canada', 'ARCH-001', 'Canada', 'Moderate', 44000, 88000, 'CAD 60k-120k/year', 'Taxable', 'Express Entry (Federal Skilled Worker); Provincial Nominee Programs; Intra-Company Transfer; LMIA-based work permits', NULL, 'CACB (Canadian Architectural Certification Board) academic assessment; then Internship in Architecture Program (IAP) with a provincial RAIC chapter; then Examination for Architects in Canada (ExAC)', 'ExAC (Examination for Architects in Canada) — 4 divisions', 'IELTS 6.0+ or CELPIP equivalent', 24, 'CACB Assessment; IAP (Internship in Architecture Program); ExAC', ARRAY['Residential/condo high-rise', 'sustainable building', 'healthcare', 'Indigenous community design'], 'Toronto, Vancouver, Calgary are highest-demand cities. Canada-UK MRA (effective May 2025) allows Canadian licensed architects faster UK registration. Filipino architects must undergo CACB academic assessment first before IAP enrollment. PR pathway very strong. Cold climate architecture skills (passive house, etc.) a niche advantage.', 'Full licensure takes 3-5 years from arrival; many Filipinos work as ''intern architects'' while in process', 'CACB; prepareforcanada.com; architecturecourses.org 2025')
