VALUES ('ARCH-001-usa', 'ARCH-001', 'USA', 'Moderate', 55000, 100000, 'USD 55k-100k/year', 'Taxable', 'H-1B (specialty worker, annual lottery); O-1 (extraordinary ability); L-1 (intracompany transfer); TN (not applicable for Philippines); Green Card via EB-2/EB-3', NULL, 'NCARB AXP (Architectural Experience Program) — minimum 3,740 documented hours; then ARE (Architect Registration Exam) — 6 divisions', 'ARE (Architect Registration Exam) — 6 divisions; administered by NCARB', 'English; TOEFL/IELTS for graduate programs', 48, 'NCARB AXP + ARE; International Applicants pathway (NCARB.org)', ARRAY['Commercial high-rise', 'healthcare architecture', 'tech campus design', 'sustainable design (LEED)', 'parametric design'], 'Most Filipino architects work as ''architectural staff'' (unlicensed) while accumulating AXP hours. H-1B lottery is a significant barrier — employer sponsorship needed. Licensed architects earn 20-30% more than unlicensed. Major markets: New York, Los Angeles, Houston, Chicago, Seattle. NCARB has reciprocity agreements with Australia/NZ — useful for those who get registered in Australia first.', 'H-1B cap lottery is a major barrier; many Filipinos spend 5-10 years before full licensure; consider Australia or Canada first for faster PR', 'NCARB 2025; AIA Compensation Report; BLS OOH 2024')
