VALUES ('ARCH-002-usa', 'ARCH-002', 'USA', 'Moderate', 55000, 105000, 'USD 55k-105k/year', 'Taxable', 'H-1B (specialty occupation); EB-2/EB-3 Green Card; O-1 for exceptional ability', NULL, 'AICP (American Institute of Certified Planners) — requires 2 years of full-time planning experience post-degree + written exam', 'AICP Certification Exam (multiple choice, 170 questions)', 'English; TOEFL/IELTS for grad programs', 24, 'AICP Certification; APA (American Planning Association) membership', ARRAY['Transportation planning', 'sustainability/climate planning', 'zoning reform', 'housing policy', 'urban design'], 'Environmental planner salary averages USD 78k in USA per Glassdoor 2026. AICP certification is the gold standard. Graduate degree (MUP/MCRP) from a PAB-accredited program greatly increases competitiveness. Many Filipino planners work for local government/consultancies in urban planning roles.', 'H-1B lottery barrier; master''s degree strongly recommended', 'Glassdoor 2026; APA')
