VALUES ('ARCH-002-international-organizations-world-bank-adb-un-habitat', 'ARCH-002', 'International Organizations (World Bank, ADB, UN-Habitat)', 'Moderate', 80000, 148000, 'USD 80k-148k/year (World Bank GF grade) + mobility premium', 'Tax-exempt (international org)', 'International org staff visa (G-series UN visa or bilateral agreement); home country nationals eligible without standard work visa', NULL, 'Masters degree in Urban Planning, Environmental Studies, or related field required; 5+ years experience for mid-level; AICP/MCIP advantageous', 'None; competitive written/technical assessment by org', 'English essential; French/Spanish/Arabic a major advantage for UN postings', 24, 'World Bank Young Professionals Program (YPP, GF level, 2-year appointment); ADB Internship + Staff Recruitment; UN-Habitat Professional Officer vacancies', ARRAY['Urban resilience', 'climate adaptation planning', 'housing policy', 'slum upgrading', 'transport planning', 'EIA for infrastructure projects'], 'World Bank GF salary USD 80k-149k + 11% mobility premium if posted abroad. ADB postings often in Asia-Pacific resident missions. PIEP (Philippine Institute for Environmental Planners) maintains international chapters in Saudi Arabia and Qatar — useful for networking. UN-Habitat specifically focuses on urban sustainable development. These roles require graduate degree and competitive application process. Postings to Africa, South Asia, MENA common.', 'Extremely competitive; master''s degree from top-ranked university is near-mandatory; 3-5 year professional experience minimum', 'World Bank Salary Grades FY2026; ADB Careers; mdbjobs.com')
