VALUES ('ARCH-003-usa', 'ARCH-003', 'USA', 'High', 55000, 143000, 'USD 55k-143k/year', 'Taxable', 'H-1B (specialty occupation for animation/game studios); O-1B (extraordinary ability in arts — strong for established artists); EB-1 (extraordinary ability Green Card)', NULL, 'Portfolio + professional work experience; no formal licensing', NULL, 'English', 18, 'O-1B visa; H-1B; studios: Disney, Pixar, Riot Games, Epic Games, DreamWorks', ARRAY['Concept art (games and film)', '2D/3D animation', 'VFX', 'character design', 'storyboarding', 'UI/UX for gaming', 'motion graphics'], 'Average concept artist salary in USA: USD 60k-123k. Top studios (Riot Games, Blizzard, Epic) pay USD 90k-200k for senior concept artists. Game Industry Career Guide reports avg video game artist salary around USD 87k in 2025. Los Angeles, Seattle, Austin, Atlanta are key hubs. Remote work common for mid-level+ positions. H-1B lottery is main barrier; O-1B more accessible for artists with strong portfolios and exhibition/professional history.', 'H-1B lottery competitive; O-1B requires demonstrable international recognition', 'gameindustrycareerguide.com 2025; ziprecruiter 2026; BLS OOH 2024')
