VALUES ('ARCH-003-japan', 'ARCH-003', 'Japan', 'Moderate', 20000, 50000, 'JPY 2.5M-6.5M/year', 'Taxable', 'Engineer/Specialist in Humanities/International Services visa (relevant to animation); Cultural Activities visa (unpaid internship/study); Specified Skilled Worker (SSW) — not applicable for arts; Philippine-Japan labor cooperation procedures apply', NULL, 'Portfolio; Japanese language (N2-N3 level strongly recommended for studio work); employer sponsorship', NULL, 'Japanese N2-N3 level for most studio roles; some international studios accept English', 18, 'Japan POLO/POEA procedures for Filipino workers; Engineer/Specialist visa', ARRAY['Anime production (in-between animation', 'key animation)', 'manga illustration', 'character design', 'game art (Nintendo', 'Square Enix', 'Bandai Namco', 'Cygames)'], 'Japan anime industry salary is modest by international standards (JPY 210k-250k/month for studio animators per Leverage Edu 2024) but iconic career path. 300,000+ Filipinos already in Japan. Key challenge: Japanese language proficiency (N2+). International game studios in Japan (Sony PlayStation Japan, Cygames, DeNA) sometimes hire English-speaking artists. Growing English-friendly opportunities in Tokyo tech/gaming sector.', 'Salary significantly lower than USA/Canada for equivalent skill level; best for career experience rather than financial optimization', 'leverageedu.com 2024; Japan POLO/POEA procedures')
