VALUES ('ARCH-004-canada', 'ARCH-004', 'Canada', 'Moderate', 33000, 60000, 'CAD 45k-82k/year', 'Taxable', 'Express Entry; Provincial Nominee Programs; LMIA-based work permit', TRUE, 'NCIDQ Certificate (National Council for Interior Design Qualification) — North American standard; requires 2 years experience + 3-part exam', 'NCIDQ Exam (3 parts); required for title ''Registered Interior Designer'' in regulated provinces (Ontario, Alberta, BC, Quebec)', 'IELTS 6.0+', 18, 'NCIDQ Certification; Interior Designers of Canada (IDC)', ARRAY['Healthcare interiors', 'commercial office', 'residential high-rise', 'hospitality', 'sustainable design (LEED ID+C)'], 'NCIDQ certification is the professional standard in Canada (and USA). Interior designers earn CAD 45k-82k. Strong healthcare interior demand post-pandemic. Toronto, Vancouver, Calgary main markets. PR pathway strong via Express Entry. IDLE qualification may require bridging assessment for NCIDQ eligibility.', 'NCIDQ exam required for title protection in regulated provinces', 'NCIDQ; glassdoor.com Canada 2025')
