VALUES ('HLT-011-usa', 'HLT-011', 'USA', 'High', 60000, 90000, 'USD 60k-90k/year (CA: up to $125k)', 'Taxable', 'H-1B (employer-sponsored specialty worker) or EB-3 (skilled worker, longer timeline)', NULL, 'ARRT (American Registry of Radiologic Technologists) certification; degree evaluated by recognized credential evaluation service', 'ARRT Radiography Exam (R) plus state licensure; modality certifications (CT, MRI, MRT) available', 'English proficiency required; TOEFL/IELTS not standardized across states', 18, NULL, ARRAY['CT', 'MRI', 'Interventional Radiology (highest paying)', 'Radiation Therapy', 'Nuclear Medicine'], 'BLS median annual wage: $77,660 (May 2024); ASRT 2024 avg: $86,484. California highest: $125k. ARRT requires education equivalency evaluation. H-1B is competitive; EB-3 requires employer sponsorship. Associate degree or higher required for ARRT.', 'Entry-level positions competitive; specialized modality (CT, MRI, IR) technologists in high demand.', 'BLS OOH 2024, ARRT 2025, DirectShifts 2025')
