VALUES ('HLT-012-usa', 'HLT-012', 'USA', 'High', 60000, 87000, 'USD 60k-87k/year (CA: up to $125k)', 'Taxable', 'H-1B (employer-sponsored) or EB-3 (skilled worker Green Card); respiratory therapist on Schedule A for EB-3', NULL, 'NBRC CRT (Certified Respiratory Therapist) then RRT (Registered Respiratory Therapist); education equivalency evaluation required', 'NBRC CRT exam (entry-level MCQ) then RRT (advanced MCQ + clinical simulation); state licensure required', 'English proficiency; state-specific requirements', 18, NULL, ARRAY['Critical Care/ICU RT', 'Neonatal-Pediatric Specialist (NPS)', 'Sleep Medicine', 'Pulmonary Rehabilitation'], 'BLS median annual wage: $80,450 (May 2024). Projected 12% growth 2024-2034. Foreign RT must have education evaluated as equivalent to US degree. NBRC CRT is entry credential; RRT is advanced. California, New York, Texas highest paying states. Travel RT: $2,040/week average.', 'ICU/critical care RTs highly valued; general hospital RTs more competitive.', 'BLS OOH 2024, NBRC 2025, SmartSalaryGuide 2025')
