VALUES ('HLT-013-usa', 'HLT-013', 'USA', 'Very High', 73000, 107000, 'USD 73k-132k/year', 'Taxable', 'H-1B (specialty occupation, MS-level CCC-SLP) or EB-3; TN visa for Canadians', NULL, 'ASHA CCC-SLP (Certificate of Clinical Competence in Speech-Language Pathology); most employers require MS degree', 'PRAXIS II SLP Exam (ETS) for CCC-SLP; state license required separately', 'English proficiency inherent to practice', 24, 'ASHA CCC-SLP certification pathway', ARRAY['Autism Spectrum Disorder (ASD)', 'Dysphagia/Feeding', 'Voice', 'Traumatic Brain Injury', 'AAC (Augmentative/Alternative Communication)', 'Pediatric Language'], 'ASHA median salary (2025): ~$95,000-107,000. BLS median (May 2024): $95,410. Top 10% earn $132,850+. MS degree required for ASHA CCC-SLP and most hospital/school positions. PH BS SLP holders may need to complete a US MS-SLP program for full eligibility. School-based SLP growing rapidly. Pediatric ASD driving demand.', 'School-based SLP positions (lower pay) easier to enter; hospital clinical positions more competitive with MS required.', 'ASHA 2025, BLS 2024, Pepperdine SLP Guide 2026')
