VALUES ('HLT-013-canada', 'HLT-013', 'Canada', 'High', 72000, 100000, 'CAD 90k-138k/year', 'Taxable', 'Express Entry (Federal Skilled Worker, TEER 1); Provincial Nominee Programs', NULL, 'SAC (Speech-Language & Audiology Canada) certification + provincial SLP college registration', 'SAC Certification exam; provincial college registration exam (e.g., CASLPO in Ontario)', 'IELTS 6.5-7.0', 18, 'SAC International Affiliate pathway', ARRAY['Pediatric Language', 'Dysphagia', 'ASD', 'Fluency', 'Voice', 'Neurogenic Communication'], 'Average hourly rate CAD 66.67 (~CAD 138k/year); senior SLPs earn $110k+ USD. Master''s degree is standard Canadian entry requirement. PH BS SLP graduates may need credential evaluation. SAC has mutual recognition arrangements. Strong demand in schools and healthcare.', NULL, 'SpeechTherapies.ca 2025, Liricare 2025, Coursera CA 2026')
