VALUES ('OTH-007-usa', 'OTH-007', 'USA', 'High', 45000, 110000, 'USD 45k-110k/year (entry: $45k-65k; senior biotech: $90k-110k+)', 'Taxable', 'F-1 (student) then OPT/STEM OPT then H-1B or O-1; EB-2/EB-3 for permanent roles', NULL, 'Degree evaluated by WES; MS or PhD preferred for research roles; ASCP certification for lab roles', 'ASCP (American Society for Clinical Pathology) BOC exam for medical lab scientist roles; no exam for general research', 'TOEFL 90+ or IELTS 6.5 for graduate school', 48, 'NIH Intramural Research Program; NSF Graduate Fellowships', ARRAY['Biomedical Research', 'Bioinformatics', 'Drug Discovery', 'Clinical Trials', 'Genetic Counseling (requires MS)'], 'Entry-level research assistant: $45k-65k. Bioinformaticians: up to $110k. Bioprocess engineers: $90k+. STEM OPT gives 3 years of post-graduation work authorization. US biotech VC funding grew 70.9% in 2025 Q2-Q3 — strong hiring expected. NIH and major universities hire international researchers.', 'PhD-level positions are competitive; industry (biotech/pharma) often pays more than academia.', 'Ichor.bio Life Science Salaries, BiotechJobs UK salary, NIH 2025')
