VALUES ('OTH-007-united-kingdom', 'OTH-007', 'United Kingdom', 'High', 32000, 65000, 'GBP 25k-52k/year (entry —25k; research scientist —41k; bioinformatics —52k)', 'Taxable', 'Student visa (for MS/PhD) then Graduate Route visa (2-year post-study work) then Skilled Worker visa', NULL, 'Degree recognition via UK ENIC; IBMS registration for biomedical scientist NHS roles', 'IBMS (Institute of Biomedical Science) registration exam for NHS biomedical scientist roles', 'IELTS 6.5-7.0', 36, 'UK Research and Innovation (UKRI) studentships', ARRAY['Genomics', 'Drug Discovery', 'Clinical Research', 'Regulatory Affairs'], 'Entry-level biomedical science roles GBP 25k-40k; Research Scientist GBP 41k; Bioinformatics Scientist GBP 52k. Graduate Route visa (2-year post-study work) is key advantage. Oxford, Cambridge, UCL, Edinburgh are major research hubs. AstraZeneca, GlaxoSmithKline, Wellcome Sanger Institute — major employers.', NULL, 'Indeed UK, ApexLearning.org.uk 2025, IBMS')
