VALUES ('OTH-014-australia', 'OTH-014', 'Australia', 'Very High', 62000, 113000, 'AUD 87k-185k/year (avg AUD 119k)', 'Taxable', 'Temporary Skill Shortage (subclass 482) then Employer-Nominated Scheme (186) for PR; or Skilled Nominated (190)', NULL, 'AVBC (Australasian Veterinary Boards Council) skills assessment for migration; state veterinary board registration', 'AVBC assessment process; may require supervised practice period if degree not in AVBC mutual recognition list', 'IELTS 7.0 in each band', 12, 'AVBC Skills Assessment for Migration', ARRAY['Large Animal (cattle', 'sheep', 'horses) — highest demand; Small Animal; Exotic Animals; Aquaculture'], 'Average AUD 119,124/year; entry AUD 87k-100k; experienced AUD 148k-185k. Active shortage with TSS visa used extensively. Rural and regional areas have strongest demand and best incentive packages. Veterinarian Salary Survey Australia Jan 2026: median A$111k rising 11% annually.', 'Urban companion animal practices more competitive; rural/large animal practices urgently needed.', 'VetClinicJobs.com 2025, AVBC, VeterinaryJobsMarketplace AU Jan 2026')
