VALUES ('OTH-014-usa', 'OTH-014', 'USA', 'High', 90000, 135000, 'USD 90k-135k+/year', 'Taxable', 'H-1B (employer-sponsored) or EB-3; J-1 exchange visitor for training; TN visa for Canadians', NULL, 'NAVLE + ECFVG (Educational Commission for Foreign Veterinary Graduates) for non-AVMA accredited degrees; PAVE alternative pathway', 'NAVLE (North American Veterinary Licensing Exam); ECFVG program for foreign graduates', 'English proficiency required; TOEFL for ECFVG', 24, 'ECFVG (AVMA) pathway for foreign veterinary graduates', ARRAY['Companion Animal', 'Zoo/Exotic Animal Medicine', 'Food Animal', 'Research Veterinarian', 'Equine'], 'USA mid-range salary $135k (2024). Entry level $90k for small animal GPs. Specialist vets (surgery, internal medicine, dermatology) earn $150k-200k+. ECFVG pathway is the primary route for non-AVMA-accredited degree holders. Process includes clinical proficiency exam. Strong but lengthy Green Card pathway.', 'Specialty positions very competitive; general practice in rural areas most accessible for internationally trained vets.', 'GlobalVetSalaryReport 2026, AVMA ECFVG, TempusVeterinary 2025')
