VALUES ('IT-001-australia', 'IT-001', 'Australia', 'High', 52000, 130000, 'AUD 80,000—200,000/yr', 'Australian taxable income (progressive; 32.5% bracket from AUD 45k—120k)', 'Temporary Skill Shortage (TSS) subclass 482 — ICT occupations on MLTSSL/STSOL: Software Engineer (261313), Systems Analyst (261111), ICT Project Manager (135101), Database Administrator (262111), Network Administrator (263111); employer sponsorship required; skills assessment by ACS (Australian Computer Society); Skilled Independent (subclass 189) — points-tested, no sponsor needed, invitation via SkillSelect; Skilled Nominated (subclass 190) — state nomination adds 5 points', NULL, 'ACS Skills Assessment — BS CS from Philippine universities assessed as comparable to Australian bachelor''s; positive assessment needed for PR pathways; 482 does not require ACS assessment', 'None for software engineering', 'IELTS Academic 6.0+ (or equivalent PTE/TOEFL) for skilled migration — Filipino applicants rarely need significant prep', 12, 'TSS 482 ICT stream, Subclass 189 Skilled Independent, Subclass 190 State-Nominated, ACS Skills Assessment', ARRAY['Cloud infrastructure', 'Cybersecurity', 'Agile/DevOps', 'FinTech', 'Government digital transformation (APS Digital Professionals)'], 'Australia''s tech market is concentrated in Sydney, Melbourne, and Brisbane. Government Digital Transformation Agency (DTA) actively recruits tech professionals. Major employers: Atlassian (HQ Sydney), WiseTech Global, REA Group, Canva, Commonwealth Bank tech division, NAB Labs, Telstra. Starting salaries AUD 80k—95k in Sydney; Melbourne slightly lower. Australia''s 2025 net migration target remains high (~185k skilled) and ICT occupations remain on the shortage list. The ACS assessment is rigorous — allow 3 months. Points test: age (25—32 = 30 pts), English (superior = 20 pts), overseas work experience, ACS assessment, state nomination = typically 75—85 points total for competitive Filipino applicants.', 'Sydney and Melbourne tech markets had layoffs in 2023—2024. Government and healthcare-adjacent tech roles remained more stable. Regional cities (Brisbane, Canberra) have lower competition.', 'Department of Home Affairs Skilled Occupation Lists 2025; ACS Skills Assessment guide 2025; Seek.com.au salary data 2025')
