VALUES ('IT-001-united-arab-emirates', 'IT-001', 'United Arab Emirates', 'High', 30000, 85000, 'AED 110,000—312,000/yr (tax-free)', 'Tax-free income (UAE has no personal income tax; note: salary in AED, not USD)', 'UAE Employment Visa sponsored by employer (standard 2-year work permit); Dubai Tech Hub (DIFC/GITEX ecosystem) — large tech employer concentration; UAE Golden Visa (10-year residency) for tech professionals with salary AED 30,000+ or as skilled employee in specialized tech occupations', NULL, 'BS CS degree + transcript (attested by DFA, UAE Embassy, MOFA) — Emirates authorities accept Philippine degrees; no additional licensing exam for tech roles', 'None for software engineering', 'English — working language for tech sector in UAE; Arabic not required', 4, 'UAE Employment Visa, Dubai Future Accelerators, GITEX employer recruitment, UAE Golden Visa', ARRAY['Smart city tech (Dubai Smart Government)', 'FinTech (DIFC FinTech Hive)', 'AI (UAE AI Strategy 2031)', 'Cybersecurity (Etisalat/e&', 'du)', 'Cloud infrastructure'], 'UAE is the fastest physical relocation pathway for Filipino CS grads. Dubai and Abu Dhabi have large tech ecosystems: e& (formerly Etisalat), du Telecom, Emirates NBD tech, Careem (Uber subsidiary), talabat, Amazon Middle East, Microsoft Gulf, Oracle Middle East. Tax-free salaries mean AED 15,000/month (~$4,900/month) is worth roughly $7,000—$8,000 in a taxed country. Large Filipino IT community in Dubai (estimated 50,000+ IT professionals). No path to permanent residency — treat as temporary deployment for savings and experience. UAE Vision 2031 and Dubai Economic Agenda D33 are generating significant tech investment.', 'No PR pathway. Oil price volatility affects government tech spending. Large Indian and Pakistani IT diaspora creates very competitive talent pool. Negotiate salary carefully — initial offers are often below market.', 'DIFC tech sector employment data 2025; UAE MOHRE wage data; Gulf IT salary surveys 2024-2025')
