VALUES ('IT-002-canada', 'IT-002', 'Canada', 'High', 55000, 120000, 'CAD 75,000—165,000/yr', 'Canadian taxable income', 'Global Talent Stream Category B — Cyber Security Analysts on Global Talent Occupations List (NOC 21220); 2-week processing; Express Entry FSW for NOC TEER 1/2 cybersecurity roles', NULL, 'WES credential assessment; CISSP, CISM, CEH recognized; Communications Security Establishment (CSE) — government roles require Canadian citizenship', 'None for private sector', 'IELTS 6.0+ for PR; English-speaking for employment', 12, 'Global Talent Stream, Express Entry, CyberNB (New Brunswick cyber cluster), Rogers Cybersecure Catalyst (Toronto Metropolitan University employer network)', ARRAY['Cloud security (Toronto FinTech hub)', 'OT/ICS (Alberta energy sector)', 'AI security', 'SOC operations'], 'Canada''s cybersecurity sector is anchored in Ottawa (government/defense suppliers), Toronto (financial), and New Brunswick (CyberNB cluster). Major private employers: RBC CIBC TD cybersec, Bell Canada, CGI Group, Sievert Group, Fortinet Canada. Canadian Communications Security Establishment (CSE) and RCMP cybercrime units are government employers requiring citizenship. Cybersecurity Center of Excellence in Guelph, Ontario is growing. Pay is lower than USA but PR pathway is faster and more predictable.', 'Canadian tech market 2024 correction affected entry-level roles. Focus on certifications and practical CTF/lab experience.', 'ISED Canada Cybersecurity Task Force Report 2024; CyberNB workforce data 2025; Glassdoor Canada cybersecurity 2025')
