VALUES ('IT-003-remote-global', 'IT-003', 'Remote (Global)', 'High', 24000, 72000, 'USD paid internationally', 'Taxable in Philippines', 'No visa needed', NULL, 'ArtStation portfolio (animation/VFX), itch.io game portfolio (game dev), GitHub for game engines, Unity/Unreal certification', NULL, 'English', 6, 'Upwork, Fiverr (lower-tier), ArtStation jobs board, remote contracts via indie game studios, crowdfunded game dev (Kickstarter teams), Concept Art Association freelance network', ARRAY['2D/3D character animation (Blender/Maya)', 'Motion graphics (After Effects)', 'Indie game development (Unity)', 'Mobile game development (Unity mobile)', 'UI/UX for games'], 'Filipino animators and game developers are actively sought as remote contractors by US, European, and Australian indie studios. Rates are lower than local US rates but negotiable with strong portfolio. Philippine animation outsourcing has been active since the 1990s (Fil-Cartoons, Top Draw Animation) — there is a deep talent pool and international contacts to tap. Mobile game development (hyper-casual, casual F2P games) is the most accessible remote game dev pathway — Unity mobile, Fyber, IronSource advertising SDK experience is marketable. VFX remote work is less common as large VFX houses typically require on-site compositing pipelines.', 'Fiverr and low-end platforms commoditize animation. Avoid race-to-bottom pricing. Build direct client relationships and specialize in a niche (character rigging, VFX, UI animation).', 'ArtStation State of the Industry 2024; Animation Magazine global outsourcing survey 2024; GDC Game Developer Survey 2025')
