VALUES ('IT-003-singapore', 'IT-003', 'Singapore', 'Moderate', 28000, 65000, 'SGD 38,000—88,000/yr', 'Singapore taxable income', 'Employment Pass (EP) — SGD 5,000/month threshold; for junior animators/game devs below threshold: Tech.Pass not applicable; some start on Training Employment Pass', NULL, 'Portfolio + degree; Imda TechSkills Accelerator for endorsed tech roles; some studios require game engine certification', NULL, 'English', 9, 'MDA (Infocomm Media Development Authority) Games Industry Grant, IMDA Digital Media Fund, Regional tech/game studio Singapore hubs', ARRAY['Mobile game development', 'Esports production', 'Animation for advertising and media', 'AR/VR development'], 'Singapore has a growing but modest game development scene compared to Canada or USA. Key employers: Ubisoft Singapore (Skull and Bones production hub), Bandai Namco Asia, Sea Group (Garena, game publisher), Gumi Asia, Mighty Bear Games, XREX, local indie studios. IMDA funds game development through Singapore Media Fund. Singapore is a regional hub for Southeast Asian game publishing and distribution. Good as a stepping stone — entry salaries lower than North America but English-speaking, nearby Philippines, no language barrier, and strong Filipino community. EP salary threshold (SGD 5,000/month) may be too high for junior game developers — studios may hire on local Employment Pass or secondary visa categories.', 'Singapore game market is small. Most major international studios use Singapore as Asian HQ for business, not large development teams. Game dev roles are relatively limited compared to FinTech or software engineering.', 'IMDA Singapore Games Ecosystem Survey 2024; Ubisoft Singapore hiring data; Sea Group investor reports 2025')
