VALUES ('IT-004-united-arab-emirates', 'IT-004', 'United Arab Emirates', 'High', 25000, 75000, 'AED 92,000—276,000/yr (tax-free)', 'Tax-free income', 'UAE Employment Visa sponsored by employer; large Filipino IT community in Dubai (telecom, banking, consulting); UAE Golden Visa for experienced IT professionals at AED 30,000+/month', NULL, 'BS IT degree + transcript (DFA-apostilled); cloud certs (AWS/Azure); ITIL 4 for service management roles; PMP for IT PM roles; Cisco CCNA/CCNP for network roles in telecom sector', NULL, 'English — working language for UAE tech sector', 4, 'UAE Employment Visa, Dubai Digital Authority IT roles, Abu Dhabi Digital Authority (ADDA) e-government programs, Smart Dubai initiatives', ARRAY['IT systems administration', 'Network administration (Cisco/Juniper)', 'ERP systems (SAP', 'Oracle)', 'IT project management', 'Cloud migration projects'], 'UAE is the fastest physical relocation pathway for BS IT graduates. Large Filipino IT professional community in Dubai/Abu Dhabi. Key employers: du Telecom, Emirates Group IT, ADNOC IT, Etisalat (e&), Abu Dhabi National Insurance, Dubai Islamic Bank IT, PricewaterhouseCoopers Middle East, Deloitte ME. ERP system roles (SAP Basis Admin, Oracle DBA, Salesforce Admin) are particularly in-demand in UAE as Vision 2030 digital transformation continues. Salaries are tax-free but buying power in Dubai is lower than it appears due to high rent. Park-and-pivot strategy applies: work in UAE 3—5 years, save aggressively, then apply for Canada Express Entry or Australia 189.', 'UAE IT market is competitive — large talent pool from India, Pakistan, Egypt. Negotiate salary carefully. Avoid illegal brokers — work only through POEA-accredited agencies for legitimate overseas employment contracts.', 'Gulf IT Salary Survey 2024-2025; UAE MOHRE employment data; DIFC technology employment reports 2025')
